  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 235 AM CST Mon Nov 16 2026\n\nWinds are expected to become southerly by Tuesday afternoon, where \nthey are expected to remain through the remainder of the work week, \nallowing for a warming trend across the area, with highs climbing to \nthe mid to upper 70s by the end of the week. Another cloudy day is \nexpected Tuesday, primarily across the Permian Basin, Lower Trans \nPecos, and southeast New Mexico due to the moist southerly flow. \nAs the week progresses, an approaching upper level trough is \nexpected to allow southerly to southwesterly winds to remain over \nthe region, bringing continued cloud cover and a low (10-20%) \nchance of isolated showers across the Permian Basin and Lower \nTrans Pecos. As the upper- level trough lifts to the northeast, a\ncold front will move through the region Saturday \nafternoon/evening into Sunday morning, bringing cooler \ntemperatures and low rain chances across the Lower Trans Pecos. \nLows are expected to remain around the 40s and 50s, with warmest \nlows on Thursday and Friday nights.\n\nBynum",
